# The flat end of a reel drum: a sixteen sided disc of radius 1.
#
# Sixteen because the drum has sixteen facets and the two have to meet: a
# twelve sided cap on a sixteen sided drum leaves four wedges of daylight
# down the side of every reel.
#
# Authored facing -Z, the same way facet.obj is, so the game stands it up
# with a yaw of plus or minus 90 degrees and each end faces outward.
mtllib drum.mtl
o cap
v 0.000000 0.000000 0.000000
v 0.000000 1.000000 0.000000
v 0.382683 0.923880 0.000000
v 0.707107 0.707107 0.000000
v 0.923880 0.382683 0.000000
v 1.000000 0.000000 0.000000
v 0.923880 -0.382683 0.000000
v 0.707107 -0.707107 0.000000
v 0.382683 -0.923880 0.000000
v 0.000000 -1.000000 0.000000
v -0.382683 -0.923880 0.000000
v -0.707107 -0.707107 0.000000
v -0.923880 -0.382683 0.000000
v -1.000000 -0.000000 0.000000
v -0.923880 0.382683 0.000000
v -0.707107 0.707107 0.000000
v -0.382683 0.923880 0.000000
usemtl drum
f 1 3 2
f 1 4 3
